menu "Kids firmware"

    comment "A single enabled app builds a single-purpose device: the"
    comment "launcher is dropped and that app opens straight from boot."
    comment "The default is hanzi only; turn the others on as needed."

    config KIDS_APP_HANZI
        bool "Build the hanzi app (stroke order + pinyin search)"
        default y
        help
            Stroke-order animation plus T9 pinyin lookup over the full
            stroke-data character set (~9.5k characters). Costs about 7.9 MB
            of flash for the stroke blob plus the fonts, and is the only app
            that allocates significant PSRAM (canvas, candidate thumbnails
            and the pinyin index, roughly 700 KB).

    config KIDS_APP_MATH
        bool "Build the math app (arithmetic)"
        default n
        help
            Two-choice arithmetic within 100. The cheapest of the three:
            only the two digit fonts and its icon, well under 300 KB.

    config KIDS_APP_ENGLISH
        bool "Build the english app (picture and sound words)"
        default n
        help
            Picture-and-sound vocabulary. The word blob is 4.1 MB at 24
            units and 7.0 MB at all 40. Control that with
            tools/english_pipeline/build_english_data.py --pack-units N,
            which is a separate axis from this switch. All three apps
            together still fit the 15.9 MB partition.

    comment "Partition layout is picked under Partition Table, not here:"
    comment "partitions.csv gives all the flash to the app, while"
    comment "partitions-with-storage.csv keeps a 4.9 MB FAT partition."
    comment "The firmware detects which one it booted with at runtime."

endmenu
